{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789841851,"nonce":"KWyVn2Lz0RvpTovOCHNDT44yYvU=","message":"Kind segregation landed in e13241b. Byte buffers (hlp_alloc_bytes, so every string), value arrays (hlp_alloc_array with a non-pointer element type) and an HDLL's MEM_KIND_NOPTR through hl_gc_alloc_gen bump through their own blocks: a second per-thread region in the Tlab, a second locked bump region, a second recycle-span list, and Block.noptr set when a block is taken from the free list and cleared when it is freed. scan_allocation_shared returns at once for an object in a noptr block; protect_kept_blocks skips them, which removes the EFAULT hazard for recv/pipe reads into a long-lived buffer. Runtime table gains gc_alloc_noptr/alloc_locked_noptr, RT_VERSION 2 (no consumer outside std).\n\nGates on the NUC: conformance 1372/1372 on interp/hybrid/jit/aot, parity 3 modes + aot_smoke green, std unit tests incl. a new one that the kinds never share a block. Corpus A/B against 922dda3 (7 reps, interleaved, 44/44 OK): every row inside the noise band, the string/json rows -1..-3%, nothing worse outside the bimodal-noise rows.\n\nMarking effect: the corpus barely collects (0 collections on stdlib/json rows), so a synthetic with 50MB of live Bytes plus 200k live small arrays shows it: mark 11.5-15.9ms -\u003e 9.7-15.4ms per collection, pause total ~135 -\u003e ~124ms over 11 collections. The bytes were ~2-3ms of scan per collection; the rest is marking the 200k live arrays, which is what sticky marks are for.\n\nRemaining for the generational half: the dirty bits are recorded but not consumed. Next is the sticky-mark collection itself: keep mark bits across a minor collection, treat protected-and-clean blocks as already marked and not to be traced, trace from roots + dirty blocks (scanned whole), sweep only unprotected blocks. Every decision it needs is now in place: per-block kind, per-block protected/dirty state, and a barrier whose cost is below noise.","files":null}]}